      <div class="proc-doc__title">Determination under Title 70 regarding Richard Dent</div>
      <div class="proc-doc__issued">Issued in New York City on the 14th of October, 1962. For public release.</div>

      <h3>Section 1: Examination</h3>
      <p>So that nothing bearing on his death is lost, altered or concealed, the Department of Culture shall secure the records of the Office of the District Attorney for the period of his tenure. The Office of the District Attorney shall produce on demand every record, correspondence, order and log of that period. Every officer and employee of that office shall answer fully when questioned. No one shall disclose that he was questioned.</p>

      <h3>Section 2: Ruling on the bar examination</h3>
      <p class="proc-doc__summary">The New York Home Rule Act gives the District Attorney no power over the qualification of attorneys and judges; that belongs to the Chief Justice in coordination with the Public Advocate. The bar examination released under the District Attorney's oversight was issued without lawful authority and is void from its issue. Every copy is withdrawn and surrendered to the Office for Information, Records, and Patents; every admission resting on it is void. No person shall be charged for having practised in good-faith reliance on it before this release. The Chief Justice and the Office shall release a new, correctly established examination.</p>

      <h3>Section 3: Safeguarding his work</h3>
      <p class="proc-doc__summary">Every release issued by the late District Attorney, or by his office, during his tenure is taken into safekeeping and withdrawn from circulation and from effect. Copies held by any office, school, association, library or publisher shall be surrendered. Use or circulation of a stricken release without the permission of the Office is Censorship Subversion. Under Article 8 of the Title 70 Act, every office of New York shall assist.</p>

      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.95rem">Nothing in the Determination attributes or excuses the act of any person in his death.</p>
    </div>
